1011. Capacity To Ship Packages Within D Days

A conveyor belt has packages that must be shipped from one port to another within days days.
The ith package on the conveyor belt has a weight of weights[i]. 
Each day, we load the ship with packages on the conveyor belt (in the order given by weights). 
We may not load more weight than the maximum weight capacity of the ship.
Return the least weight capacity of the ship that will result in all the packages on the conveyor belt being shipped within days days.

Explanation:

We dont know the number of days required to ship these weights with given capacity .
(Whatever capacity we are considering we dont know how long will it take to ship). 
First calculate it becuase with that only we can compare with the threshold days.
The core logic lies in finding the number of days it takes with the given capacity.

Starting of find the actual days needed. set it as number of daysto 1 and current load to 0;
if the current_load+ weight[i] < capacity then add more weight
else > capacity, then move weight[i] to the next day and increament day count (days++);
return days;

with this we know the number of days for a given weight.

Next comnsider all the weights.
left set as ->This is the max weight of weights because we need minimum this weight to ship it individually
right set as -> This is the sum of weight of all weights. If we are carrying all in a single day
imaginary array of the possible weights.
Apply BS on these possible weights, check with mid. 
If actuall_days_needed(weights,mid)<=days, ans=mid and reduce right to mid-1 cause anything above than 'mid''s weight's days will do it.
else left=mid+1;

Code:
class Solution {
    public int shipWithinDays(int[] weights, int days) { // function for min_weight
        int left=-1; // This is the max weight of weights because we need minimum this weight to ship it individually

        for(int weight:weights){
            left=Math.max(left,weight);
        }

        int right= 0; // This is the sum of weight of all weights. If we are carrying all in a single day
        for(int weight:weights){
            right+=weight;
        }

        int ans=-1;

        while(left<=right){
            int mid=(left+right)/2; // Capacity considering now
            if(actuall_days_needed(weights,mid)<=days){
                ans=mid;
                right=mid-1;
            }
            else{
                left=mid+1;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }

    public int actuall_days_needed(int[] weights, int threshold_capacity){
        int days=1; int load=0;
        for(int weight:weights){
            if(load+weight<=threshold_capacity){
                load+=weight;
            }
            else{
                days++;
                load=weight;
            }
        }
        return days;
    }
}
